#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105411 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "e598ad1e-cee5-5d5f-b2a9-c067e4625cf6" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Angles and Magnitudes"}] :question/id #uuid "1a24b403-754c-5424-8182-8cad3487deed" :question/math-academy-id "e-15606" :question/problem "Suppose $\\mid \\,\\mathbf{a}\\,|=13$ and the angle between vectors $\\mathbf{a}$ and $\\mathbf{b}$ is $\\theta = \\dfrac{2\\pi}{3}$. Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = | \\, \\mathbf{a} \\, | \\cos   \\theta \\\\  & = 13 \\cos   ( \\frac{2 \\pi}{3} ) \\\\  & = 13 \\cdot  ( - \\frac{1}{2} ) \\\\  & = - \\frac{13}{2} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105412 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "91691448-c59a-56dc-a775-d4e9c3297036" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Scalar Projection Using Components"}] :question/id #uuid "da8a1521-86cc-5747-88a7-e2ec56010c11" :question/math-academy-id "e-15607" :question/problem "Let $\\mathbf{a}=\\langle 3,3,-1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{b}=\\langle 2,-7,0 \\rangle$. Find the scalar projection of $\\mathbf{a}$ onto $\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Using the formula for the scalar projection, we obtain\n\n$$\\begin{array}{rl}{\\text{comp}}_{\\mathbf{b}} \\, \\mathbf{a} & = \\frac{\\mathbf{a} \\cdot  \\mathbf{b}}{| \\, \\mathbf{b} \\, |} \\\\  & = \\frac{{a}_{x} {b}_{x} + {a}_{y} {b}_{y} + {a}_{z} {b}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2} + {b}_{y}^{2} + {b}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & = \\frac{3 \\cdot  2 + 3 \\cdot  ( - 7 ) + ( - 1 ) \\cdot  0}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2} + ( - 7 {)}^{2} + {0}^{2}}} \\\\  & = - \\frac{15}{\\sqrt{53}} .\\end{array}$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105413 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a51e317c-f6b3-5704-afb4-bdfc79f1176f" :knowledge-point/title 